title ALES123 — Lotus's stereo_insert_silence: opening a silent gap carried into stereo, both channels in lockstep
prompt Continue the recurring baton (prin recur) on the ALES/Lotus edge, Lindy-first crux-first; approve my own design rounds; send each finished increment as its own signed round; stop at custody gates.
think Fourth lap of the session's recur run. ALES122's recommend line named insert_silence (grows, ClipFull) and shift (length holds) as the two clean next lifts. insert_silence is the tighter crux — it is the growth-twin of the silence just landed at ALES122 (silence written in place, length holds; silence made room for, length grows), so lifting it right after silence_span lets the growth/hold distinction bind the two.
think Read mono insert_silence (ALES109): faults BadRange (at > len) and ClipFull (count > buf.len - len). Confirmed buf: [max_clip]i16, so buf.len == max_clip and the stereo guard matches stereo_duplicate's own ClipFull guard exactly. Same validate-both-before-either shape as ALES120: check at and the grow once against the shared length, then run mono insert_silence per channel, each pre-validated to succeed.
think Wrote the design read, module, witness. Four laws proven on metal: stereo insert law (each channel == ALES109 byte for byte, both grown by count, gap all zero), balance/invariant law (left.len == right.len, both grown by count, head and tail-append), inverse law (== original after ALES117's stereo_cut(at, count) — the lossless round-trip lifted from mono ALES109), atomicity/degenerate law (a refusal leaves both untouched and balanced, count 0 identity, at=len appends, a full clip ClipFull).
obs The inverse law is the round's keystone — it ties stereo_insert_silence to stereo_cut over their public APIs so the open-then-remove round-trip is provably lossless, the exact contrast with ALES108's lossy shift the mono ALES109 already drew, now in stereo. Witness GREEN first run; tame_style_check clean.
loom witness=ales_stereo_insert_silence_witness result=GREEN laws=4 channels=2
file lotus/stereo_insert_silence.rye ALES123 — stereo_insert_silence lifts ALES109's mono insert_silence to a StereoClip, validate-both-before-either, four laws.
